TailGauge began as a port of the first-party Tailscale panel plugin that ships
with Omarchy 4 (Quattro), moved off Hyprland/Quickshell onto KDE Plasma 6 and
GNOME Shell, with an Omarchy widget built back on the result.

Upstream: https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy (MIT, Copyright (c) David
Heinemeier Hansson), branch `quattro`, `shell/plugins/panels/tailscale/` and
the `omarchy-tailscale-*` helpers.

The codebase has since been rewritten in Rust, and none of the files that
carried upstream's code survive it. What is owed is the lineage rather than a
file: the behaviour this panel reproduces - how a status is read, how accounts
and exit nodes are grouped, how Mullvad regions are folded together, when
Taildrop is offered - was worked out there first, and the MIT notice in
LICENSE-MIT travels with it.

`omarchy/arzaroth.tailgauge` is a third-party plugin. It does not replace or
modify `omarchy.tailscale`, and is not endorsed by the Omarchy project.

